// D-CONF-PLANE1/D-CONF-NAME1 (card #1517): `outputs:` names the runnable
// artifact and the file that defines it — `entry: run` means "the file at
// this package's root with a top-level `fn run`", found by declaration, not
// by a `main.jet`/`run.jet` filename convention. This package deliberately
// has neither: its entry lives in `service.jet`. `jet run` (JIT) and
// `jet build` (AOT) both resolve it the same way (I9) — rename `service.jet`
// without updating `entry:` and the build stops naming the missing file,
// it does not silently fall back to a convention name.
name: "outputs_build_demo"
version: "0.1.0"
outputs: .{ demo: .Executable.{ entry: run } }
